
- Affected when the player is moving, traveling, changing location, or navigating terrain.
  Short movements (30 feet, crossing a room, climbing a wall) still count if they
  matter mechanically (e.g. provoking opportunity attacks, difficult terrain).
- Affected when the action is about proximity to specific world elements: approaching
  or moving toward NPCs, creatures, objects, or landmarks (e.g. a lake, a door, a
  tree, the goblins). "I approach the goblins", "I move toward the lake", "I get
  closer to the altar" all affect traversal because they change the character's
  position relative to those elements.
- destination: the name of a STORY LOCATION the player is actively traveling toward,
  only when they have not yet arrived. Set to null if:
  - the player is already at or inside the destination (e.g. "I enter the tavern" when
    the player is already in the village — the tavern is not a new story-level destination)
  - the action is a short movement within the current location (crossing a room, approaching
    an NPC, climbing a wall)
  - the target is an entity or landmark rather than a named story location
  Only set destination when the player is undertaking meaningful travel to reach a
  new story location they have not yet reached.
